Native Amiga LoadView interrupt regression
=========================================

Selected by test-graphics-amiga-m68k and its quick target. Build independently
with test-graphics-loadviewinterrupts or test-graphics-loadviewinterrupts-quick.

After blanking the OS view, simulate a hardware takeover by clearing VERTB,
then clearing all interrupt enables. A repeated LoadView(NULL) must restore
VERTB and the master enable without altering other interrupt or DMA enables.
With an outer Disable(), VERTB must be restored while the master stays off.
Restore hardware interrupts before WaitTOF even on failure, so the old ROM
reports its failures rather than hanging the test. Confirm the frame counter
advances after each case and restore the caller's view on exit.

The old implementation fails four of fifteen checks. No emulator-only
register reads or production library-vector patches are used.
